 "note": [
  "Take Root API is egress-blocked from this container (curl to api.takeroot.bible returns 000). The Kulish text was fetched instead from the ebible mirror on raw.githubusercontent.com (gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/ukr_pan/usfm), all 66 books / 31,082 verses, and every span marked mined was lifted from it with a script rather than typed.",
  "Derived by measurement, not from a translator's report: each quoted span was byte-matched against the Kulish verse it cites, blind only to our own quotation marks and a sentence-initial capital. 90 of 102 distinct references matched; the rest are the review queue and each carries its reason.",
  "Kulish's own nested quotation marks are „ … ‟ (U+201F). They are preserved as „ … “ to match the shipped uk corpus, which carries zero U+201F. Punctuation only — no letter moves.",
  "VERSE NUMBERING: Kulish diverges from the author's Bible in two places this book cites. Genesis 3 runs one behind — the enmity-with-the-serpent verse the author cites as 3:15 (ch04, block 3) is Kulish's 3:14, and Kulish's 3:15 is the woman's curse. 1 Samuel 24 likewise runs one behind (ch14). Both citations are printed as the author printed them; a reader checking them in Kulish lands on the wrong verse.",
  "REFERENCE LABEL: this edition cites Hebrews as «Євреїв», not Kulish's own running head «Жидів». The shipped uk corpus is already split (Жидів in godliness.uk and baptism-with-the-holy-spirit.uk, Євреїв in clothed-with-strength-and-dignity.uk and jesus-himself-2.uk), so both are attested. This book is a sustained exposition of Hebrews 11 — the name is on almost every page and is a chapter title — and «жид» is pejorative in modern Ukrainian, where Kulish's 1905 title predates the shift. Only the editorial label changed; Kulish's own words are untouched. Flagged for review."
